### P9-04 progress — explicit pull facade

- Confirmed the initial `cargo check -p rocketmq-classic-consumer --locked` stop was caused by the root facade adding the consumer crate without a matching `Cargo.lock` entry. Ran `cargo check -p rocketmq-classic-consumer --offline` to refresh the lockfile and compile without network access. This exposed implementation issues (missing Java `ExpressionType.isTagType` behavior, private class-filter router visibility, and `SharedValue` conversion); fixed those and removed the sibling-private `OffsetTable` placeholder test.
- Added `PullConsumerConfig`, `PullConsumerError`, explicit `PullConsumer` methods, lifecycle registration/unregistration, namespace wrapping for the consumer group and queues, per-queue Broker suggestion routing, slave flag handling, filter hooks, offset-store selection, and explicit update/read/persist APIs. Pull responses are decoded through `PullAPIWrapper`; pulling does not update or persist offsets.
- Corrected broker-name header encoding to Java's inherited `RpcRequestHeader.bname` field for pull and offset RPCs, confirmed against the pinned 5.5.1 source. Updated the existing remote-offset scripted test to assert `bname`.
- Added config and pull-input unit checks plus a loopback NameServer/Broker test covering routed queues, TAG request fields, decoded FOUND, all three non-FOUND pull statuses, unit-mode hooks, no implicit offset mutation/persistence, explicit offset update/read/persist, and consumer lifecycle.
- Verification: `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-consumer --locked` passed (24 unit, 4 offset, 1 pull-facade, 7 pull-result tests); `cargo check -p rocketmq-classic --locked` passed; `cargo fmt --all -- --check` and `git diff --check` passed. P9-V03 live-Broker validation remains pending for Phase 19.
- P9-04 is ready for its independent commit after final staged-diff review.

